Federal Geographic Data Committee and U.S. Geological Survey. Digital Cartographic Standard for Geologic Map Symbolization, FGDC-endorsed 2006 standard. [Official standard, status, and downloadable materials](https://www.fgdc.gov/standards/projects/geo-symbol/).

Read the introduction and the complete symbol sections needed for contacts, orientation, folds, faults, uncertainty/location, and the actual map being studied. Distinguish a symbol's defined meaning from what a particular observation establishes. Compare with the regional map's own legend rather than assuming one national convention applies unchanged everywhere.

The official catalogue identifies the 2006 endorsement and publication resources. A direct USGS publication endpoint returned automated-access denial; the official FGDC page was accessible. Preserve the actual publication/component notices before reuse. Identity/status and authorized source route checked on 29 October 2026. No symbols, fonts, or style libraries are embedded in a Sand or copied into this trail.

